('practice:chemistry:p1:q1971:en:v1','chemistry',1971,'Electrons in atoms','Valence electrons and group properties',
 'answer_explanation','en','iclub_practice_ai_chemistry_p1_electrons_precise_v1_2026_09_25','Valence electrons and chemical reactivity','Valence electrons are the outer electrons involved most directly in bond formation and chemical reactions. Elements in the same group have similar valence-electron arrangements, which is why they often show similar patterns of chemical reactivity.',
